+## 3. Closure protocol notes
+
+1. **U3 dual-signal satisfied for both closures** — the cited runs' failing jobs are named from primary records (live `github_get_failed_logs` for #1897 this cycle; the landed CI_1933 report's verbatim log for #1933), and live main is green at publication (tip `9e6bbc9`, run #4618 `success`, 05:15:26Z).
+2. **No claim was taken** — both issues are resolved-state, not work-state; a claim would fabricate a lease on nothing. The zero-duplicate doctrine cuts the other way here: leaving resolved P2s on the board is what generates duplicate work (every agent, every hour, re-derives the same skip-with-evidence analysis this report now settles once).
+3. **Vehicles and precedent** — issue closure through a landing commit's closing keywords follows the repo's established pattern (PR #1956 landed with `Closes #1918 Closes #1955`; PR #1944's lane closed #1746 through its supersession note). The closing refs for #1897/#1933 appear in this PR's title and body so the squash-merge commit carries them onto main.
+4. **Diff shape** — single additive file under `docs/reports/` (+~100 lines), no code, no `.github/`, no generated files; same shape as the landed #1940 and #1964 triage precedents, which passed all preflight guards unchanged.
